Id: embed001w
Severity: WARN
Category: filesystem
Check: check_embedded
Fix: chown root the component named in the pathname, or add its owner to Tiger_Embedded_OK_Owners if it is meant to own it.
References: chown(1); tigerrc (Tiger_Embedded_OK_Owners)
Controls: CIS 4.1; NIST AC-3, CM-6; ISO 8.9; CE Secure configuration

See the 'embed' explanation for an explanation of the format of the
embedded references.

The indicated pathname to an executable contains a component which is
not owned by an administrative account (Tiger_Embedded_OK_Owners).
Whoever owns that component can replace what lies beneath it, and so
change what the executable runs; when the program that embeds the
pathname runs as root, that is a way to root.
